# Project Shell

Four Cygwin stage trees (see `scripts/build-config.ts`, default under
`D:/CI-Tools`):

- `msys64-stage1`, `msys64-stage2`, `msys64-stage3`, `msys64-stage3-mingw`

For bash, makepkg, pacman, and other POSIX/MSYS work, use the bash for the
stage you are on:

`<stage-dir>/msys64/usr/bin/bash.exe --login -i`

Set `MSYS=winsymlinks:native`, `MSYSTEM=CYGWIN`, `CHERE_INVOKING=1`, and prepend
`<stage-dir>` and `<stage-dir>/msys64/usr/bin` to `PATH`.

Use the matching `MSYS2-CYGWIN-STAGE*` profile from `.vscode/settings.json`
when possible. Do not use bare `bash` or `sh` from Windows `PATH` (may resolve
to WSL).

Do not run bare `cmd` or `cmd /c` when MSYS `usr/bin` is on `PATH`; use
`cmd.exe` or `%COMSPEC%` if Command Prompt is needed.
